     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is 2 to 2.5 times the usual maximum: 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. A dose that high carries a real risk of lactic acidosis and severe GI toxicity, even with normal renal and hepatic function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum for immediate-release)\n- **1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals** (2,000 mg/day)\n- **500 mg PO three times daily with meals** (1,500 mg/day)\n- **1,700 mg/day divided**, for example 850 mg twice daily\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. If 1,700 mg three times daily is what you intend, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed the dose."
      }
     ],
